question:
Answer the following multiple choice question. The entire content of your response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of {letters}.

{question}

{choices}

Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is the 'ability to consummate' concept subject to Material Adverse Effect (MAE) carveouts?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: 'Company Material Adverse Effect' means any effect, change, event, circumstance, or condition that, individually or in the aggregate, materially adversely affects the business, financial condition, or results of operations of the Company and its Subsidiaries, taken as a whole, or prevents, materially delays, or materially impairs the ability of the Company to consummate the transactions contemplated by this Agreement; provided, however, that none of the following shall be deemed to constitute a Company Material Adverse Effect for purposes of the business condition clause: (i) changes in general economic conditions or in the industries in which the Company operates; (ii) changes in laws, regulations, or accounting principles; (iii) acts of God, natural disasters, or pandemics; (iv) changes in the Company's stock price or trading volume; (v) any failure by the Company to meet financial projections; and (vi) any actions taken by the Company that are required by this Agreement or with the written consent of the Parent. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the exclusions set forth in this definition shall not apply to the ability of the Company to consummate the transactions contemplated hereby.' (Pages 45-46)\nAnswer:
